{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And if the household be too little for a lamb.</b> Too little for eating the lamb, for if the people of the household are few, he and his neighbor shall take it." "במכסת. A portion; and so המכס לי׳ (Numbers 31:37) is the portion that each one takes; like it: 'י׳ is the portion of my lot and my cup' (Psalms 16:5), also תכסו. It is of the double-letter forms (מפעלי הכפל), the doubled letter being absent both from the word במכסת and from המכס. Now he said המכס on the pattern of וממר ליולדתו (Proverbs 17:25), which is likewise of the double-letter forms."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :notes {1 "Resolved the abbreviation י׳ to י׳ (YHWH) based on the cited verse from Numbers 31:37, where the phrase reads המכס ליהוה; translated the abbreviation consistently as YHWH per voice rules."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:33:27.646995025Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}